{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 149,
    "dDurationMs": 4601,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In our everyday world, we're used to absolute,\ndeterministic predictions: throw a ball in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4750,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the air, and it'll fall along an ellipse;\nleave your umbrella parked on the street,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8950,
    "dDurationMs": 3419,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and when you come back, it's still there,\njust one umbrella."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12369,
    "dDurationMs": 3921,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Quantum physics is not like this - because\nquantum mechanics doesn't allow us to make"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16290,
    "dDurationMs": 2371,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "absolute predictions about the future."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18661,
    "dDurationMs": 3499,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It only predicts the likelihoods of different\noutcomes to happen, and doesn't say anything"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22160,
    "dDurationMs": 1629,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about which one will happen."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23789,
    "dDurationMs": 3791,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"Well,\" you might say, \"that's the same with\nthe weather - the weatherman only tells you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27580,
    "dDurationMs": 4109,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what the chance of rain is; he can't tell\nyou whether or not it will rain.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31689,
    "dDurationMs": 3251,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But maybe the weatherman just doesn't have\ngood enough knowledge of exactly where all"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34940,
    "dDurationMs": 4090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the air and water molecules in the world\nare, nor a good enough model of how they interact"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39030,
    "dDurationMs": 3970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or a fast enough computer to simulate all\nof their bajillion interactions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43000,
    "dDurationMs": 3830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Maybe in principle, if he had enough data\nand a fast enough computer, his weather model"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46830,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "could tell you exactly where every raindrop\nwould fall."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50030,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51030,
    "dDurationMs": 4060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This reasonable idea, that if you just had\nmore data you could explain everything, is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55090,
    "dDurationMs": 3020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the classical, deterministic view of the universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58110,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And for a while, many physicists, including\nEinstein, thought the same had to be true"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62250,
    "dDurationMs": 4550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with quantum mechanics - maybe we just didn't\nhave enough information to put into our quantum"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66800,
    "dDurationMs": 4470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "models; maybe there were classical variables\nthat were hidden from us and our experiments,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71270,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "inputs that explained everything perfectly\nwith no need for quantum mechanics and its"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74790,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"I'll give you 50/50 odds on the cat being\ndead\" mentality."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78480,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Except, it turns out that we can actually\ntest whether or not this sort of classical,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82200,
    "dDurationMs": 4070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "underlying explanation of quantum physics\ncan exist even in principle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86270,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The details are a topic for another video,\nbut the experiments tell us…"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90170,
    "dDurationMs": 4150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there is no classical, everyday, underlying\ndescription of quantum mechanics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94320,
    "dDurationMs": 4150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this means, Einstein, that the universe\nis quantum mechanical whether you like it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 98470,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with a 50% chance, or not."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 102610,
    "dDurationMs": 4630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ps, I'm excited to announce that MinutePhysics\nis now supported by MinutePhysics t-shirts."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107240,
    "dDurationMs": 21359,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Get yours now at dftba.com/minutephysics and\ndon't forget to be awesome."
    } ]
  } ]
}
